Dictionary in Python (Easy Explanation)
A Dictionary in Python is a data type used to store data in key–value pairs.
Think of it like a real dictionary:
Key = Word
Value = Meaning
Syntax
dictionary_name = {
    "key1": value1,
    "key2": value2,
    "key3": value3
}
Example
student = {
    "name": "Preethi",
    "age": 19,
    "course": "BCA"
}

print(student)
Output
{'name': 'Preethi', 'age': 19, 'course': 'BCA'}
Characteristics of Dictionary
Stores data in key-value pairs.
Keys must be unique.
Values can be duplicated.
Dictionaries are mutable (can be changed).
Created using {}.
Accessing Values
student = {
    "name": "Preethi",
    "age": 19,
    "course": "BCA"
}

print(student["name"])
print(student["age"])
Output
Preethi
19
Adding a New Item
student = {
    "name": "Preethi",
    "age": 19
}

student["course"] = "BCA"

print(student)
Output
{'name': 'Preethi', 'age': 19, 'course': 'BCA'}
Updating a Value
student = {
    "name": "Preethi",
    "age": 19
}

student["age"] = 20

print(student)
Output
{'name': 'Preethi', 'age': 20}
Deleting an Item
student = {
    "name": "Preethi",
    "age": 19,
    "course": "BCA"
}

del student["course"]

print(student)
Output
{'name': 'Preethi', 'age': 19}
Dictionary Methods
1. keys()
Returns all keys.
student = {"name":"Preethi","age":19}
print(student.keys())
2. values()
Returns all values.
print(student.values())
3. items()
Returns key-value pairs.
print(student.items())
4. get()
Gets the value of a key safely.
print(student.get("name"))
5. update()
Updates the dictionary.
student.update({"course":"BCA"})
print(student)
6. pop()
Removes a specified key.
student.pop("age")
print(student)
7. clear()
Removes all items.
student.clear()
print(student)
Looping Through a Dictionary
Print Keys
student = {"name":"Preethi","age":19,"course":"BCA"}

for key in student:
    print(key)
Print Values
for value in student.values():
    print(value)
Print Keys and Values
for key, value in student.items():
    print(key, ":", value)
Example Program
student = {
    "name": "Preethi",
    "age": 19,
    "course": "BCA"
}

print("Student Details")
print("Name:", student["name"])
print("Age:", student["age"])
print("Course:", student["course"])

student["college"] = "XYZ College"

print("\nUpdated Dictionary")
print(student)
Output
Student Details
Name: Preethi
Age: 19
Course: BCA

Updated Dictionary
{'name': 'Preethi', 'age': 19, 'course': 'BCA', 'college': 'XYZ College'}
